{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1149409-advice-on-building-a-artifact","id":1149409,"title":"Advice on building a artifact","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-13T07:55:11-07:00","id":1149409,"title":"Advice on building a artifact","content":"I am planning a Werewolf campaign set in the Caribbean where the PCs are chasing after a surprisingly elusive artifact collector who has recently gotten his hands on a Garou artifact. I am seeking advice on developing the artifact and how to make a pack made out of different tribe members interested in recovering it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T09:00:47-07:00","id":1149436,"title":"","content":"If your pack is made of treasure hunters then there is no other explanation needed. There are lots of fetishes that have been lost and never recovered. What rank are the shifters in question? if they already have rank they may have a reputation that actually has other Septs call on them to retrieve the item. If its just a hunch that this person has it and no hard proof, they may not want to dedicate any of their own resources to chasing it down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T13:35:26-07:00","id":1149515,"title":"","content":"Garou Artifact sounds like a fetish. While you might be tempted to make the fetish more powerful than usual, I don't think that is a key. Instead, develop a legend around it. What great heroes used it? What great story tells of its creation? Think of legendary weapons like Excalibur or the Spear of Destiny, or legendary objects like the Holy Grail or the Cauldron of Plenty. For inspiration see this<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_mythological_objects\" target=\"_blank\"> list of objects</a>. A well developed story about it will be much more of a hook than boosting its powers.<br /> <br /> As for getting your PC pack involved, there are various possibilities. Maybe in the course of this fetish's existence, it has been wielded by Garou of many tribes. And those Garou happen to be ancestors of multiple pack members. Or maybe the fetish is particularly tied to the Totem Incarna of their pack, and the quest comes to them via their pack totem. Or the pack is an Anruth pack going from sept to sept seeking adventure, and the sept leader of one assigns the pack this quest. Or simply because this is Werewolf, the pack's theurge has some kind of vision, reads the tea leaves, or has some other kind of enigmatic sign that the pack must be the ones who find it (and of course has to overcome other Garou packs who also are seeking this).<br /> <br /> Following mystic signs, discovering fetishes and lost Garou lore, and holding onto important fetishes are the kind of things that Garou earn renown for, so you may not need much more of a hook. Just make sure the fetish description and legend is something your players will find appealing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T17:42:30-07:00","id":1149576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1149409-advice-on-building-a-artifact?p=1149515#post1149515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou Artifact sounds like a fetish. While you might be tempted to make the fetish more powerful than usual, I don't think that is a key. Instead, develop a legend around it. What great heroes used it? What great story tells of its creation? Think of legendary weapons like Excalibur or the Spear of Destiny, or legendary objects like the Holy Grail or the Cauldron of Plenty. For inspiration see this<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_mythological_objects\" target=\"_blank\"> list of objects</a>. A well developed story about it will be much more of a hook than boosting its powers.<br /> <br /> As for getting your PC pack involved, there are various possibilities. Maybe in the course of this fetish's existence, it has been wielded by Garou of many tribes. And those Garou happen to be ancestors of multiple pack members. Or maybe the fetish is particularly tied to the Totem Incarna of their pack, and the quest comes to them via their pack totem. Or the pack is an Anruth pack going from sept to sept seeking adventure, and the sept leader of one assigns the pack this quest. Or simply because this is Werewolf, the pack's theurge has some kind of vision, reads the tea leaves, or has some other kind of enigmatic sign that the pack must be the ones who find it (and of course has to overcome other Garou packs who also are seeking this).<br /> <br /> Following mystic signs, discovering fetishes and lost Garou lore, and holding onto important fetishes are the kind of things that Garou earn renown for, so you may not need much more of a hook. Just make sure the fetish description and legend is something your players will find appealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThanks for the advice. Two ideas I got so far is a legendary klaive that reportedly glows green when in the presense of wyrm taint, ala the Hobbit. Or, it is something connected to Turtle, the Croatoan's former totem. I was planning on having the Collector buy the item from either a estate sale or from a antiquities auction being hosted by one of Pentex's subsidiaries. If I go the Pentex route, how do you think Pentex could've gotten their hands on the artifact and why would they sell it in a auction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}